    "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\nComputes `MultimodalRotaryEmbedding`'s RoPE angles with an elementwise product instead of a K = 1 matmul, so they stay exact when TF32 is allowed for fp32 matmuls. Details in the issue #8842.\n\n```python\n# before\ninv_freq_expanded = self.inv_freq[None, None, :, None].expand(3, seq.shape[1], -1, 1)\nseq_expanded = seq[:, :, None, :].float()\nfreqs = (inv_freq_expanded @ seq_expanded).transpose(2, 3)\n# after\nfreqs = seq[..., None].float() * self.inv_freq\n```\n\nElementwise computation in the latter means we reach torch kernels, and not cublas. Output is bit identical to the current code with TF32 off. It is also faster (not the aim of this PR): one forward on B300 takes 42.4 µs instead of 52.6 µs at 32,768 positions, and 92.1 µs instead of 182.9 µs at 131,072.\n\nNew test `test_angles_exact_when_tf32_allowed`: it runs the module with TF32 allowed and not allowed, compares with an fp64 reference, and requires both outputs to be identical.\n\nTest results:\n| `TORCH_ALLOW_TF32_CUBLAS_OVERRIDE` | this PR | current `main` |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 (container default) | 13 passed | new test fails at 4,096 / 16,384 / 21,845; the other 10 pass |\n| 0 | 13 passed | same 3 failures |\n\nOnly measured on B300. On GPUs where cuBLAS picks the exact kernel for these shapes, the new test also passes on current `main`.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nLinked issue: Fixes #8842\n\n## Code provenance\n\nNo code was copied. Hugging Face transformers made a similar change independently in [huggingface/transformers#49265](https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/pull/49265)\n\n## Contribution process\n\n### Pre-checks\n\n- [x] I have added relevant unit tests\n- [ ] I have added relevant functional tests (not added: a one-line numerics change, covered by the unit test)\n- [ ] If this PR adds or changes a GPU kernel (Triton, `jit_fuser`/`torch.compile`, CUDA extension, TE or external-library dispatch, or a scatter/index accumulation), I have added or updated its bit-exact determinism test and registered it in `tests/unit_tests/determinism/kernels/manifest.py` ([guide](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/blob/main/docs/developer/determinism/testing.md)) (not applicable: the change removes a cuBLAS call and adds no kernel; `tools/check_kernel_determinism_coverage.py` passes)\n- [ ] I have added proper typing to my code [Typing guidelines](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html) (N/A)\n- [ ] I have added relevant documentation (not applicable)\n- [x] I have run the [autoformatter.sh](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/blob/main/tools/autoformat.sh) on my PR\n",
